  "full_text": "Make his fight on the hill in the early day. Constant chill deep inside. On they run through the endless gray. For the right, yes, but who's to say? For a hill men would kill why they do not know. Stiffened wounds test their pride. Men of five still alive through the raging glow. Gone insane from the pain that they surely know. Stranger now are his eyes to this mystery. Here's the silence so loud. Black and roared. Deaf and roared. The need to be. Fills the air with the ruthless cry. Wait. I don't know. I got to print these lyrics out. Crack of dawn. Something like that. Let's get Mr. Garth. The clouds of the valley shall be sweet unto him. And every man shall draw after him. As there are innumerable before him. How then can ye offer me? How then comfort ye me in vain? Seeing in your answers there remains falsehood. See, it's like, why does the... Why does he fight for the hill? He does not know. He's just a kid. Wait.",
